hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16240","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Furat from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us while we were discussing the Hour, and said: What are you mentioning? They said: We are mentioning the Hour. He said: It will not stand until you see ten signs: the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, and Yajuj and Majuj, and three land-swallows: a swallow in the east, a swallow in the west, and a swallow in the Arabian Peninsula, and the last of that a fire emerging from its direction driving the people to their gathering place. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: A word has dropped."
"16241","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel enters upon the sperm drop after it settles in the womb by forty nights, and Sufyan once said: or fifty and forty nights, and says: O Lord, what, wretched or blessed, male or female? So Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, says, and they write; then they say: What, male or female? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, says, and they write; then his deed and his trace and his calamity and his provision are written; then the scroll is folded, and neither is added to what is in it nor decreased."
"16242","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Furat from Abu al-Tufayl from Abu Sarihah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in an upper room while we were beneath it talking. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked down upon us and said: What are you mentioning? They said: The Hour. He said: The Hour will not stand until you see ten signs: a swallow in the east, a swallow in the west, a swallow in the Arabian Peninsula, and the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, and Yajuj and Majuj, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden moving the people on. Shubah said: I heard him, and I think he said: It stays with them where they stay and rests at midday with them where they rest."
"16243","Shubah said: And a man narrated this hadith to me from Abu al-Tufayl from Abu Sarihah, not raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): One of these two men said: The descent of Isa son of Maryam, and the other said: A wind casting them into the sea."
"16244","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Furat from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from an upper room while we were discussing the Hour, and said: The Hour will not stand until you see ten signs: the rising of the sun from its west, the smoke, the Beast, the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj, the emergence of Isa son of Maryam, and the Dajjal, and three land-swallows: a swallow in the west, a swallow in the east, and a swallow in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire emerging from the bottom of Aden driving or gathering the people; it spends the night with them where they spend the night and rests at midday with them where they rest."
"16245","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah and Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of the Negus. He said: Then he said: Pray over a brother of yours in other than your land."
"16246","He said: Abd al-Samad and Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said: Al-Muthanna narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them one day and said: Pray over a companion of yours who died in other than your land. They said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Suhmah the Negus. And Azhar said: Sahmah. And Azhar said: Abu al-Tufayl al-Laythi, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid al-Ghifari."
"16247","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day and said: Pray over a brother of yours who died in other than your land. They said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Suhmah the Negus. So they stood and prayed over him."
